    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I was wondering whether it's possible to implement `Allman` style for brackets.\r\n\r\nI am writing C# where the default convention is putting brackets on separate lines. \r\n\r\nLet's say I have such method signature:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\n    public void TestMethod() {}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs it possible to put both brackets on separate lines, either directly when inserting the open bracket or hitting enter when inside brackets?\r\n\r\nDesired result:\r\n```csharp\r\n    public void TestMethod() \r\n    {\r\n\r\n    }\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I was wondering whether it's possible to implement <code class=\"notranslate\">Allman</code> style for brackets.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am writing C# where the default convention is putting brackets on separate lines.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let's say I have such method signature:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-cs notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    public void TestMethod() {}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-k\">public</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">TestMethod</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible to put both brackets on separate lines, either directly when inserting the open bracket or hitting enter when inside brackets?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Desired result:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-cs notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    public void TestMethod() \n    {\n\n    }\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-k\">public</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">TestMethod</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> \n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "I was wondering whether it's possible to implement Allman style for brackets.\nI am writing C# where the default convention is putting brackets on separate lines.\nLet's say I have such method signature:\n    public void TestMethod() {}\nIs it possible to put both brackets on separate lines, either directly when inserting the open bracket or hitting enter when inside brackets?\nDesired result:\n    public void TestMethod() \n    {\n\n    }",
