            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "With 'mini.pairs' - I am afraid the answer is a no. It deliberately [acts as an equivalent of `<CR><C-o>O`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pairs.html#minipairs.cr), i.e. does not affect the left character.\r\n\r\nA possible solution here might be to use [`MiniKeymap.map_multistep()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-keymap.html#minikeymap.map_multistep) with a custom step. To do that only inside C# files, create a `~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/csharp.lua` filetype plugin with the following content:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nif _G.MiniKeymap then\r\n  -- Act only when cursor is between `{}`\r\n  local is_inside_braces = function()\r\n    local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\r\n    local col = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)[2]\r\n    return line:sub(col, col + 1) == '{}'\r\n  end\r\n  -- Mock a sequence of keys that produce an Allman style\r\n  -- NOTE: It is not perfect, as there might be issues with indentation and\r\n  -- trailing whitespace. Adjust it to fit the use case better\r\n  local allman_action = function() return '<Left><CR><Right><CR><CR><Up><Tab>' end\r\n  local allman_step = { condition = is_inside_braces, action = allman_action }\r\n\r\n  -- Create a buffer-local mapping that doesn't remap (to be able to use `<CR>` in the output\r\n  -- without infinite recursion\r\n  local opts = { remap = false, buf = 0 }\r\n  MiniKeymap.map_multistep('i', '<CR>', { 'pmenu_accept', allman_step, 'minipairs_cr' }, opts)\r\nend\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">With 'mini.pairs' - I am afraid the answer is a no. It deliberately <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pairs.html#minipairs.cr\" rel=\"nofollow\">acts as an equivalent of <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;CR&gt;&lt;C-o&gt;O</code></a>, i.e. does not affect the left character.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A possible solution here might be to use <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-keymap.html#minikeymap.map_multistep\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniKeymap.map_multistep()</code></a> with a custom step. To do that only inside C# files, create a <code class=\"notranslate\">~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/csharp.lua</code> filetype plugin with the following content:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"if _G.MiniKeymap then\n  -- Act only when cursor is between `{}`\n  local is_inside_braces = function()\n    local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\n    local col = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)[2]\n    return line:sub(col, col + 1) == '{}'\n  end\n  -- Mock a sequence of keys that produce an Allman style\n  -- NOTE: It is not perfect, as there might be issues with indentation and\n  -- trailing whitespace. Adjust it to fit the use case better\n  local allman_action = function() return '&lt;Left&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;Right&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;Up&gt;&lt;Tab&gt;' end\n  local allman_step = { condition = is_inside_braces, action = allman_action }\n\n  -- Create a buffer-local mapping that doesn't remap (to be able to use `&lt;CR&gt;` in the output\n  -- without infinite recursion\n  local opts = { remap = false, buf = 0 }\n  MiniKeymap.map_multistep('i', '&lt;CR&gt;', { 'pmenu_accept', allman_step, 'minipairs_cr' }, opts)\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">_G</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">MiniKeymap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Act only when cursor is between `{}`</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">is_inside_braces</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">line</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_get_current_line</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">col</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_win_get_cursor</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>)[<span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>]\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">line</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">sub</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">col</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">col</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">+</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>{}<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Mock a sequence of keys that produce an Allman style</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> NOTE: It is not perfect, as there might be issues with indentation and</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> trailing whitespace. Adjust it to fit the use case better</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">allman_action</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Left&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;Right&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;CR&gt;&lt;Up&gt;&lt;Tab&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">allman_step</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">condition</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">is_inside_braces</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">allman_action</span> }\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Create a buffer-local mapping that doesn't remap (to be able to use `&lt;CR&gt;` in the output</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> without infinite recursion</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">remap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">buf</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span> }\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniKeymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_multistep</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>pmenu_accept<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">allman_step</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>minipairs_cr<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "With 'mini.pairs' - I am afraid the answer is a no. It deliberately acts as an equivalent of <CR><C-o>O, i.e. does not affect the left character.\nA possible solution here might be to use MiniKeymap.map_multistep() with a custom step. To do that only inside C# files, create a ~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/csharp.lua filetype plugin with the following content:\nif _G.MiniKeymap then\n  -- Act only when cursor is between `{}`\n  local is_inside_braces = function()\n    local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\n    local col = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)[2]\n    return line:sub(col, col + 1) == '{}'\n  end\n  -- Mock a sequence of keys that produce an Allman style\n  -- NOTE: It is not perfect, as there might be issues with indentation and\n  -- trailing whitespace. Adjust it to fit the use case better\n  local allman_action = function() return '<Left><CR><Right><CR><CR><Up><Tab>' end\n  local allman_step = { condition = is_inside_braces, action = allman_action }\n\n  -- Create a buffer-local mapping that doesn't remap (to be able to use `<CR>` in the output\n  -- without infinite recursion\n  local opts = { remap = false, buf = 0 }\n  MiniKeymap.map_multistep('i', '<CR>', { 'pmenu_accept', allman_step, 'minipairs_cr' }, opts)\nend",
